config CITRONICS_DLN2
	tristate "Citronics Limeboard I/O"
	depends on USB && GPIOLIB && I2C && SPI_MASTER && IIO && COMMON_CLK
	select MFD_CORE
	select GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
	select IIO_BUFFER
	select IIO_TRIGGERED_BUFFER
	help
	  The Limeboard's STM32 running the Limeboard I/O firmware: its
	  Raspberry Pi style header as a GPIO chip, I2C and SPI buses and
	  an ADC. The firmware speaks the Diolan DLN-2 protocol; this is
	  the kernel's DLN-2 driver set as one separate module that binds
	  to the firmware's USB ID only.

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module
	  will be called citronics-dln2.
